From 19bc1d3448c75dca74b78a9cd07ff66f2dff3734 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 11:36:11 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] vieww-text: an example that times the system font scan
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The step-by-step startup trace (8f8997f) caught the wait_loop hang on the
affected laptop: the last line before 20 s of silence was `window made
visible`, and `system fonts loaded` never came. Between them are only the
frame log, the frame driver and `driver.use_system_fonts()` — the full
fontdb scan of every font fontconfig lists, run on the main thread before
a window's first frame, in every process.

That fits every observation: it fails on the first scenario after an
11-12 minute build (the build evicts the font files from the page cache;
the same run's window creation took 1.2 s instead of 30 ms), and later
scenarios — and every warm manual run — pass, because the fonts are
cached by then.

examples/font_scan.rs times exactly that scan (fontdb's, and the
FontStore vieww builds), so it can be measured cold and warm on the
machine where it hangs. Here: 130 ms for 238 files on first run, 8 ms
warm.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Nd3Ehrf9ktGu82K38kGEjH
