From aa372d1a0bcf4d6306978b7e98e7298ab34bcbc0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 11:47:50 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Windows draw before the system font scan finishes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The wait_loop hang, found. The step-by-step startup trace on the affected
GNOME/Wayland laptop ended at `window made visible`, and `system fonts
loaded` never printed: `driver.use_system_fonts()` — a full fontdb scan
of every font fontconfig lists, run on the main thread before a window's
first frame, in every process — overran the test's 20 s deadline. It
only happened on the first scenario after an 11-12 minute build (which
evicts the font files from the page cache; window creation in the same
run took 1.2 s instead of 30 ms) and never on a warm run. A user
launching an application after a reboot pays the same, so this is a
startup fix, not a test fix.

- vieww-text: FontStore::system_fallback_in_background(on_ready) runs
  with_system_fallback's scan on a `vieww-font-scan` thread and calls
  on_ready when done; PendingSystemFonts::try_take()/wait() build the
  store on the owning thread (FontStore keeps Rc caches and is not
  Send; the scanned fontdb::Database is). Same faces, same order, so
  the same tie-breaking — tested. with_system_fallback is unchanged in
  behaviour and now documents its cost.
- vieww-render: FrameDriver::use_system_fonts_in_background(on_ready);
  `drive` adopts a finished scan first thing — set_fonts (relayout of
  every object), invalidate (full repaint), request_frame — so a loop
  woken by on_ready with nothing else to do still shows the new fonts.
  Tested, and mutation-checked (without the frame request the adoption
  never paints). fonts_pending() for callers and tests.
  use_system_fonts() stays blocking for headless callers.
- vieww-platform-winit: the App uses the background scan and wakes its
  loop from the scan thread (UserEvent::Wake). First frame here: 16 ms
  after the window opens rather than after the scan.

Traces: `startup: system font scan started`, and the driver prints
`system fonts adopted` under VIEWW_TRACE_FRAMES.

vieww-text 118/118, vieww-render 509/509, vieww-platform-winit 145/145
(wait_loop 5/5 three times under Xvfb); clippy, fmt, docs clean.

